 "title": "Mekedatu dam row (13-14 Nov 2026): Karnataka CM D.K. Shivakumar, at the COSMOS-Mysuru planetarium opening with PM Modi present (13 Nov), asked the Centre for final clearances for the Mekedatu balancing reservoir and said 'Mekedatu has to be built in Karnataka and no one can stop it'; on 14 Nov he said TN will still get its share under the SC ruling ('It is my state, my right'); Karnataka puts the project at Rs 16,745 crore (PTI, IANS); TN CM Vijay's 7 Nov letter asked the PM to withhold clearances without co-basin consent (67.16 TMC reservoir); TN Assembly's unanimous resolution 19 June; TNCC chief Manickam Tagore called the remarks 'deeply condemnable'; DMK's Stalin asked Vijay for an all-party meeting; SC on 13 Nov 2025 rejected TN's applications as premature; 2018 verdict: 177.25 TMC a year at Biligundlu.",
